    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14191" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dis-convĕnĭo</span></b> ,
			īre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. n., to disagree; to be inharmonious,
				inconsistent</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aestuat et vitae disconvenit ordine toto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 1, 99</span></i>
			.—<i>Impers.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eo disconvenit inter Meque et te,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 14, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disconveniens deo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. de Ira D. 3, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
